# Project Tasks Must Be Included in Cross-Cutting Features

## The Issue

Assisy has two separate task types:
- `Task` (from `TaskContext`) — regular tasks on Dashboard
- `ProjectTask` (from `ProjectContext`) — tasks inside projects/sub-projects

They have different status values, priority scales, and fields. A full type merge is planned but not done yet.

## The Rule

When building any feature that shows tasks across the whole app (calendar, stats, weekly review, search, etc.), you MUST include both regular tasks AND project tasks.

Use the shared utility `projectTasksToTasks()` from `lib/mergeProjectTasks.ts`:

```typescript
import { useProjectContext } from '../context/ProjectContext';
import { projectTasksToTasks } from '../lib/mergeProjectTasks';

const { subProjects, projects, getTasksBySubProject } = useProjectContext();
const allTasks = useMemo(
  () => [...tasks, ...projectTasksToTasks(subProjects, projects, getTasksBySubProject)],
  [tasks, subProjects, projects, getTasksBySubProject],
);
```

Then use `allTasks` instead of `tasks` for any cross-cutting computation.

## Already Applied To
- Calendar.tsx
- Dashboard.tsx (weekly stats)
- WeeklyReview.tsx

## Field Mapping (ProjectTask → Task)
- `Done` → `Completed`, `In Progress`/`Backlog` → `Pending`
- `deadline` → `dueDate`
- `priority: Medium` → `High`, `effort: Medium` → `Low`
- Category defaults to `Professional`
- Title includes project name: "Task (Project Name)"
- ID prefixed with `pt-` to avoid collisions
